      <div>
        <span class="section-index">01 / History</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3">One idea.<br>One workbench.<br><em class="serif-italic">Five decades of engineering.</em></h2>
        <p class="lead mt-3">What began in 1969 as a repair and engineering workshop in Lingen has grown into one of the most specialised machine manufacturers in European trench cutter construction.</p>
        <p class="mt-3" style="color: var(--steel-700);">Today LIBA carries out design, welding, hydraulic integration and final assembly entirely in-house — under one roof, with the same family at the helm. Our machines are not consumer goods. They are working tools capable of decades of deployment — and that is the standard applied to every weld, every hose and every bearing that leaves our factory.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="media-frame"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/products/gm-180-af-detail.jpg" alt="Manufacturing at the LIBA factory in Lingen (Ems) — detail of trench cutter GM 180 AF" width="1200" height="2133"><span class="tag">Factory Lingen (Ems)</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

